---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, types } from '../site';
const subject = `Contribution to ${site.fullName}`;
const body = `Title:
What it is (guide, paper, activity, framework, discussion pack, or a reading to link to):
A few sentences on what it is for and who it is for:
How you would like to be credited (name, role, and a link if you want one):
I confirm I have the right to share this and am happy for it to be published under ${site.licence.label}: yes / no

(Attach the file, or paste the link.)`;
const mailto = `mailto:${site.contributeEmail}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;
---
<Base title="Contribute" description={`How to add a document, activity, framework or reading to ${site.fullName}: email it, with attribution.`}>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:0.5rem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
      <h1>Send it. It gets added, with your name on it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Commons grows by email. There is no upload form and no account. Send what you have and the editor will add it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:1rem">
    <div class="wrap resource">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What is welcome</h2>
        <ul>
          {Object.values(types).map((t) => <li><strong>{t.plural}.</strong> {t.blurb}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p>Anything that would help an EAP tutor or course leader engage well with AI. It does not have to be polished, and it does not have to be long. A one-page activity that works is worth more than a long document that does not.</p>

        <h2>What to include</h2>
        <p>Use the button, which opens an email with the template below, or copy the template into your own message.</p>
        <div class="template">{body}</div>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem"><a class="btn primary" href={mailto}>Email a contribution</a></p>
        <p class="small muted">Or write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contributeEmail}`}>{site.contributeEmail}</a>.</p>

        <h2>What happens next</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>The editor reads it. Expect a reply within a couple of weeks.</li>
          <li>If it is added, it gets its own page with your name and a download, under <a href={site.licence.url} rel="license">{site.licence.label}</a>.</li>
          <li>You can ask for changes or removal at any time by replying to the same thread.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Not everything sent will be published. The Commons is curated, and its usefulness depends on that.</p>
      </div>
      <aside data-pagefind-ignore>
        <div class="panel">
          <h4>Attribution</h4>
          <p class="small" style="margin:0">Contributors keep copyright. Their name, and a link if they want one, appears on the resource and in any pathway that uses it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h4>Formats</h4>
          <p class="small" style="margin:0">Word, PowerPoint or PDF for documents. A link for readings. If you have both a source file and a PDF, send both.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
